{
  format: 1
  name: string-search-needle-length-boundaries
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#expressions", "§6.5"]
  tags: ["boundary"]
  note: '''
    The two length boundaries §6.5 forces from its decomposition definitions,
    with the needle supplied as state so no expectation depends on a literal
    being special-cased:

      - the EMPTY needle decomposes every subject (`s = "" ++ s`, `s = s ++ ""`,
        `s = "" ++ "" ++ s`), so all three predicates are true — including on the
        empty subject, where p, n and r are all empty (rows e1, e2);
      - a needle LONGER than the subject admits no decomposition at all, so all
        three are false (rows e3, e4); §6.5 states the contrapositive: any true
        predicate implies size(n) <= size(s).

    Row e5 is the equality boundary between them: n = s decomposes with an empty
    p and r, so all three are true.

    Empty `text` is used only as a FIELD value, never as a `$key` (an empty text
    key is refused, §D.2), so the boundary under test is the predicate's, not the
    key encoder's.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.strbounds@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      pairs: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        subject: "text"
        needle: "text"
        starts: "= string.starts_with(.subject, .needle)"
        ends: "= string.ends_with(.subject, .needle)"
        holds: "= string.contains(.subject, .needle)"
      }
      $public: {
        pairs: { $view: ".pairs { id, starts, ends, holds, $sort: [id] }" }
      }
    }
    $data: {
      pairs: {
        e1: { subject: "512100", needle: "" }
        e2: { subject: "", needle: "" }
        e3: { subject: "512", needle: "512100" }
        e4: { subject: "", needle: "5" }
        e5: { subject: "512100", needle: "512100" }
      }
    }
  }

  steps: [
    { watch: "public.pairs", id: "w1",
      expect_init: { value: [
        { id: "e1", starts: true, ends: true, holds: true }
        { id: "e2", starts: true, ends: true, holds: true }
        { id: "e3", starts: false, ends: false, holds: false }
        { id: "e4", starts: false, ends: false, holds: false }
        { id: "e5", starts: true, ends: true, holds: true }
      ] } }
  ]
}
